app-title = CodexBar
app-comment = AI usage from CodexBar for Linux in the COSMIC™ panel
app-keywords = COSMIC;AI;Usage;Quota;

## Popup (Connecting, Unavailable, Incompatible)

connecting = Connecting to CodexBar…
not-running = CodexBar for Linux isn't running
not-running-body = This applet shows usage from the CodexBar desktop app. If it isn't installed, follow the official installation guide. If it is, open CodexBar from the app launcher.
not-responding = CodexBar for Linux isn't responding
not-responding-body = CodexBar for Linux is installed but doesn't answer, which can happen after it crashes. Restart it: quit CodexBar if it's still open, then open it again from the app launcher.
desktop-app-settings = Keep Start at login on in CodexBar Settings so usage is available after you log in, and turn off Tray icon there, since this applet replaces it.
open-install-guide = Open installation guide
check-again = Check again
incompatible = This CodexBar version isn't supported. Update CodexBar and this applet.
open-applet-page = Open applet page

